# Model Timestamps

Every database model must have `createdAt` and `updatedAt` fields. Never create a model without them.

## Do / Don't

```prisma
// ❌ BAD — no audit timestamps
model User {
  id    String @id @default(uuid())
  email String @unique
}

// ✅ GOOD — createdAt + updatedAt on every model
model User {
  id        String   @id @default(uuid())
  email     String   @unique
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt
}
```

## Checklist

- Add `createdAt` and `updatedAt` to every new Prisma model (or equivalent in raw SQL migrations).
- Use `@default(now())` for `createdAt` and `@updatedAt` for `updatedAt` in Prisma so they are set automatically.
- Include both fields in migrations when adding new tables — do not add them later as an afterthought.
- Do not omit timestamps on join/lookup tables unless there is an explicit, documented exception.
